            "The levers are the levels of prevention. <strong>Primordial</strong>: the tobacco law, the excise tax on sugar-sweetened drinks, salt reduction in manufactured foods, school food policies, the market with a place to walk. <strong>Primary</strong>: the lifestyle counselling that names the food and the day, and the hepatitis B and HPV vaccines that prevent liver and cervical cancer. <strong>Secondary</strong>: the blood pressure at every adult contact, the glucose for those at risk, the waist tape, the cervical screen, the breast examination, the foot and eye checks of the diabetic, the urine dipstick for protein. <strong>Tertiary</strong>: the stroke survivor's rehabilitation, the diabetic foot that is saved, the epilepsy that is controlled, the heart failure that is kept out of the ward.",
